## Default design system

Unless the mission above explicitly calls for a different aesthetic, build this project using the slate-blue glass design system documented below. Use exactly these tokens so the app feels cohesive with the operator's Jarvis dashboard.

### Color

- **Canvas:** `#06080C` (deep slate)
- **Glass surface:** `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)` with `backdrop-filter: blur(24px)`
- **Text primary:** `#FFFFFF`
- **Text secondary:** `#CBD5E1`
- **Text muted:** `#94A3B8`
- **Text faint:** `#7F8C9E`
- **Accent gradient:** `linear-gradient(to right bottom, #53617A, #3A445C)`
- **Border (default):** `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)`
- **Border (hover):** `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18)`
- **Status:** success `#22c55e` · warn `#eab308` · error `#ef4444`

### Typography

- Inter 400/500/600 loaded from Google Fonts with system-font fallback (`-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif`)
- **H1** 36px / 600 / -0.025em tracking / 40px line-height
- **H2** 26px / 600 / -0.025em
- **H3** 24px / 600 / -0.025em
- **Body** 12-14px / 500
- **Caption / label** 10-11px / 600 uppercase with 0.5px tracking (use this for labels on glass cards)

### Surfaces

- 24px `backdrop-filter: blur` on every panel / card / modal
- **Hero edge treatment (signature):** 1px slate gradient hairline around hero cards + primary modals. Paint it with the double-background trick:

  ```css
  .hero-card {
    background:
      linear-gradient(rgba(16, 21, 31, 0.92), rgba(16, 21, 31, 0.92)) padding-box,
      linear-gradient(to right bottom, #53617A, #3A445C) border-box;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25),
                0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
  }
  ```
- **Radii scale:** 2px, 8px, 12px, 24px, 32px, 9999px (pill)
- **Shadow stack:**
  - Soft: `0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)`
  - Card: `0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)`
  - Hero: `0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25)`

### Spacing

4px base unit. Scale: **4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32**. Card padding defaults to 16-20px. Section padding 24-48px.

### Motion

- `--motion-fast: 150ms`
- `--motion-ease: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)`
- Hover = **color change only** — no transforms, no border-beam, no decorative glows
- Any `transition:` declaration should go through these two tokens

### Ambient background (optional but recommended)

Full-bleed CSS-only dot-matrix with slow 120s drift. `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables the drift. No Three.js.

```css
#ambientBg {
  position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(circle at 18% 8%, rgba(83, 97, 122, 0.22), transparent 55%),
    radial-gradient(circle at 82% 92%, rgba(58, 68, 92, 0.28), transparent 55%),
    radial-gradient(circle, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.10) 1px, transparent 1.4px);
  background-size: 100% 100%, 100% 100%, 24px 24px;
  animation: ambientDrift 120s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes ambientDrift { to { background-position: 0 0, 0 0, 100px 100px; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { #ambientBg { animation: none; } }
```

### Buttons

- 12px radius, 11px / 500 Inter
- Primary: wears the slate gradient, `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` border, `brightness(1.1)` on hover
- Secondary: `rgba(255,255,255,0.04)` fill, `rgba(255,255,255,0.1)` border, text becomes `--text-primary` on hover

### Inputs

- 12px radius
- `rgba(255,255,255,0.04)` fill, `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` border, 14px body text
- Focus ring: `0 0 0 2px rgba(148,163,184,0.45)`

## How the team works here

- **Lead:** run the app's dev server via `cm dev announce http://jarvis:<port> --pid $!`. If the project is fullstack, use named slots: `--name frontend` + `--name api`. Expo teams use `expo start --web --host 0.0.0.0 --port 19006`.
- **Everyone:** check `cm dev url` + `cm dev creds` before browser verification.
- **Every UI task completion MUST cite browser verification** in the `cm task complete --summary` (e.g. "Screenshotted at /tmp/signup.png — new layout visible").
- Bind dev servers to `0.0.0.0`. Pick ports in 3000-3999 (frontend) / 8000-8999 (backend) / 19006 (Expo web). Avoid 3555/3556 (Jarvis) and 9222 (headless-shell).
- Full reference: `cm skill read team-dev-instance`.

